Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  MS 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   CASE  MS 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient    Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2  Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D   CHIENWEI ERIC LIAO  M D   Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D         CLINICAL DATA   Left breast cancer       FINAL DIAGNOSIS   BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   1  EXTENSIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 1  WITHIN AND BEYOND THE REGION OF  BOTH BIOPSY SITES   2  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA     NOTE  The ductal carcinoma in situ is  0 2cm from margins       GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is a 781  g  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x up to 7 5cm mastectomy specimen  with a long stitch  designating lateral and a short stitch designating superior  The overlying REMOVED_DATE  x 3 0cm ellipse of skin shows a curved healed scar  measuring 2 2cm in  length  which is located along the inferior and lateral aspects of the skin  ellipse  The nipple is inverted  The areola is grossly unremarkable  The  anterior margin is inked blue  and the posterior margin is inked black  The  anterior margin in the lower outer quadrant is disrupted over an area of REMOVED_DATE x  0 8cm  with exposure of an underlying cavity  On sectioning  the breast  parenchyma of the upper outer quadrant shows an irregular  tan pink to  gray white biopsy cavity  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm and located 1 0cm from  the nearest posterior margin and 2 0cm from the nearest anterior margin  The  cavity is lined by granulation tissue and the wall of the cavity shows  indurated fatty tissue  with foci of hemorrhage  fat necrosis  and fibrosis   Obvious tumor is not appreciated  The breast parenchyma of the lower outer  quadrant also shows a biopsy cavity  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  which is  located more centrally and is exposed at the anterior margin and 4 0cm from  the nearest posterior margin  This biopsy cavity is also tan pink to  gray white and is lined by granulation tissue  and the wall shows indurated  fatty tissue  with foci of hemorrhage and fat necrosis extending up to the  anterior margin  Obvious tumor is not identified  The breast parenchyma  between the 2 biopsy cavities is mostly fibrotic and firm and shows prominent  tan pink glandular tissue  The remaining breast parenchyma consists of admixed  fatty tissue and pink white fibrous stroma  The subareolar tissue also shows  dense fibrosis  Lymph nodes are not identified  Representative sections are  submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity in the upper outer quadrant  with adjacent breast  parenchyma and anterior and posterior margins    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrotic breast tissue  with prominent glandular tissue  between the 2  cavities  lateral breast    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity in the lower outer quadrant  with surrounding breast  parenchyma and nearest anterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nearest posterior margin from the biopsy cavity in the lower outer  quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nipple    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma away from both the biopsy cavities  medial breast      Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on Friday  REMOVED_MONTH 22   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 58 27PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses     PART   Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy       report_end  , Unchecked.
