Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 91 at 14 05 CLINICAL DATA  Metaplastic carcinoma with osteoclastic giant cells  Minor component of typical infiltrating ductal carcinoma mixed with intraductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   RIGHT   METAPLASTIC CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Most of the tumor is composed of highly anaplastic spindle and epithelioid cells  accompanied by abundant osteoclast like giant cells  In areas  the malignant spindle cells produce osteoid  A small focus  less than 1  of the total tumor  of intraductal carcinoma of the solid type is present  The accompanying report of immunoperoxidase studies from Rhode Island Hospital states the malignant spindle cells focally  stain positively for keratin and EMA  and do not stain for vimentin  These features are consistent with metaplastic breast carcinoma  It is not possible to assess the resection margins  Vascular invasion is present  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 91 at 17 51                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     Immunohistochemistry on formalin fixed paraffin embedded tissue shows that the tumor cells are positive for vimentin  muscle specific and smooth muscle specific actin  EMA and alpha 1 antichymotrypsin and are negative for keratin  S 100 and desmin  This staining pattern is consistent with myofibroblastic or smooth muscle differentiation of the tumor cells  Added by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 15                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE LOCATION REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  OUTSIDE INSTITUTION  RHODE ISLAND HOSPITAL OUTSIDE PATHOLOGIST  M S  Duwaji  M D  RHODE ISLAND HOSPITAL DEPARTMENT OF PATHOLOGY PROVIDENCE  RI  REMOVED_CASE_ID  OUTSIDE CLINICIAN  Norbert J  Craybas  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Date of Procedure  23 JUL  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Slides  17 Blocks  0   report_end  , Unchecked.
