rior   blue  and posterior   black  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6 8cm skin has an unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm nipple and areola complex  A 3 0cm well healed semi circular scar is located 0 5cm from the nipple at the 12 o clock position and an additional 3 5cm well healed linear scar is located 9 0cm from the lateral resection margin and 2 0cm from the lateral skin resection margin  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm incisional biopsy cavity with pink to hemorrhagic smooth walls  The cavity is located within 1 5cm from the nearest posterior resection margin  2 0cm from the nearest anterior resection margin  6 0cm from the nearest medial resection margin  7 0cm from the nearest inferior resection margin  8 5cm from the nearest superior resection margin  and 26 0cm from the nearest lateral resection margin  In addition  a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan yellow to focally hemorrhagic area consistent with a previous biopsy site is identified at the lateral portion of the breast  This area is within 1 0cm from the posterior resection margin  2 0cm from the superior resection margin  3 0cm from the anterior resection margin  and 5 0cm from the inferior resection margin  9 0cm from the nearest lateral resection margin  and 27 0cm from the medial resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma reveals an unremarkable white pink fibrous and tan yellow fatty tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity to nearest posterior resection margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Second biopsy site to the nearest posterior resection margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma away from biopsy cavity  The axilla is dissected to reveal multiple potential tan red lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Section code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lymph node adjacent to previous biop