Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 49 CLINICAL DATA  Status post needle localization      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  CORRECTED ADDENDUM TISSUE SITE Revised by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Revised on 22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 19                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA GRADE REMOVED_DATE CM  85   EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  15   CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Edited by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 01                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 02    REVISED REMOVED_DATE    GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal an approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm ill defined  firm area with white streaks  abutting the closest inked surface  corresponding to area of architectural distortion  Area too small to be frozen  Suspicious area submitted in cassette A  the remainder of the specimen in cassettes B through J  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT  SMALL FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA BUT TOO SMALL TO BE FROZEN  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
