TE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibrofatty tissue  inked and serially sectioned proven no gross abnormalities  Representative section is submitted as I and K N  The second specimen consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibrofatty specimen  surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm irregular portion of skin  the specimen is inked  serially sectioned  to reveal no gross abnormalities and a representative section is submitted as J and O R  Resident  ARASH RADFAR  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST LEFT   ADDITIONAL LATERAL TISSUE , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 20 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM AS MEASURED ON A GLASS SLIDE  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  FOCALLY ALONG A BROAD FRONT   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  PRESENT IN ALL 11 SLIDES  INTERMEDIATE TO HIGH GRADE  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES  NOTE  Definite lymphatic and blood vascular invasion is not seen  The ductal carcinoma in situ is present in all slides and probably spans greater than 3 0cm  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 48                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is an unoriented  5 x 3 x 1 5cm portion of breast tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined  2 x 1 x 1cm  tan  gritty region abutting the resection margin at several points  A representative section is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in cassette A  The remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassettes B K  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  APPROXIMATELY 1 X 1 X 1 CM  AND INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  APPROXIMATELY 1 X 1 X 1 CM  O R  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
