Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 27 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 1  EXTENDING TO THE INKED MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS AND PRESENT AT THE MARGIN   SEE NOTE   NOTE  No blood vascular or lymphatic space invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm stellate tan white firm mass  present at inked margin  Representative section of the mass and the closest margin are frozen as FX 1 and submitted in cassette A  the rest of the mass and margin are in cassettes B through E  representative section of remaining tissues are in cassettes F through J  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST MASS  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA VERY CLOSE TO A MARGIN  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AT A MARGIN  O R  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Richard Paul Cambria  M D  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
