inely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh from the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left partial mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of breast oriented with stitches  short stitch supperior  long stitch lateral   The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a tumor mass grossly approaching the medial margin  The tumor is 2 5cm in greatest diameter  Section code  A D  mass from anterior to posterior E  tumor to closest medial margin F  representative section of normal breast Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast tissue  additional medial margin  short stitch designating the superior margin and the long stitch designating the new medial margin   is an oriented fibrofatty portion of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned from medial to lateral  There is a white  centrally located area  primarily in the lateral portion of the specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  This area is entirely submitted in cassettes M P with a representative section of normal breast in Q  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of fibrofatty tissue  There are 24 tan  rubbery nodules ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  One half of the five largest nodules are submitted in cassettes G H and the remaining nodules are submitted in cassettes I L  Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD     IN