Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 17 CLINICAL DATA  Fifty eight year old female with 1 5cm tumor with positive margins on biopsy from an outside facility  now undergoing partial mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 29                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The skin ellipse contains a vertical scar measuring 3 8cm in length  As denoted by the surgeon  a short stitch marks the superior aspect of the specimen and a long stitch marks the lateral aspect of the specimen  The specimen is inked entirely in black and then serially section from superior aspect to its inferior aspect to reveal a central hemorrhagic cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm that is within REMOVED_DATE   0 3cm of the anterolateral border of the superior portion of the breast  A predominant gray yellow area of firm consistency measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm extends to within 0 2cm of the posterolateral margin in the superior aspect of the specimen  Continuing superiorly is a firm area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm at the lateral inked margin  No other gross lesions are identified  Section code  A  biopsy cavity from mid region of specimen with skin ellipse anterior  demonstrating anterolateral margin  B  area of white thickening in superior aspect of the specimen  with posterolateral margin  C  biopsy cavity and lesion at lateral margin  with medial surface removed  D  lesion at posterolateral margin  E  biopsy cavity from mid area of specimen surface removed F G  biopsy cavity  at lateral margin of specimen  in the superior portion  H  lesion in lateral aspect of specimen I  superior margin Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael V Seiden  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
