Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 10 01 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  60    WELL TO MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATIED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  PRESENT WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  40    MIXED MICROPAPILLARY  AND CRIBRIFORM TYPE  3  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  SEPARATE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  4  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  5  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  6  SIMPLE DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  7  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCYSTS  FIBROSIS  AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  8  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  The infiltrating ductal carcinoma measures 1 5cm in greatest diameter  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The infiltrating lobular carcinoma is separate from the infiltrating ductal carcinoma and measures 0 2cm in diameter  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of pink tan fibroadipose tissue with a firm center and an area  1 5cm   of white tan gritty tissue adjacent to margin  Representative section taken as FX 1  submitted in P and the remainder of the specimen A through O  Sections L and M are adjacent to FX 1  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS  INVASIVE AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  M  Priscilla Short  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Nash  Jennifer Reports To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  History of invasive ductal and lobular carcinoma  Bow tie stitches in new cephalad  Short stitch   anterior  long stitch   lateral  posterior aspect in biopsy cavity is open  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  SPANNING 1 2CM X 1 1CM  GLASS SLIDE MEASUREMENT   ALL RESECTION MARGINS ARE NEGATIVE   0 2CM   SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 1  SMALL FOCI WITHIN THE TUMOR  ALL RESECTION MARGINS ARE NEGATIVE   0 2CM   LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   EXTENSIVE  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OUT OF 17 LYMPH NODES WHICH MEASURES 1MM IN GREATEST DIMENSION AND IS IDENTIFIED BOTH ON AN HE AND A CYTOKERATIN IMMUNOSTAIN  NO EXTRACAPSULAR LYMPHATIC EXTENSION IS IDENTIFIED  NOTE  This tumor is arising in the vicinity of the nipple and is not immediately adjacent to the biopsy cavity  The carcinoma extends into the deep dermis of the nipple  with focal pagetoid spread into the epidermis  Paget s Disease of the breast   In this region  tumor is also present within lymphatic vessels  with focal perineural invasion  When comparing this carcinoma with the patient s previous ductal and lobular carcinomas   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    the current tumor is not morphologically identical to either  This histologic discrepancy  in addition to the small foci of ductal carcinoma in situ identified within the tumor  and the fact that the tumor is not immediately next to the previous biopsy site  all raise the possibility that this tumor may represent a third primary  The invasive carcinoma is positive for e cadherin  which is consistent with an invasive ductal carcinoma  There is no evidence of residual invasive lobular carcinoma  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  There are several cellular proliferations within the ducts in this specimen   the cells of which show negative staining with an e cadherin stain  supporting that these proliferations are lobular carcinoma in situ rather than ductal carcinoma in situ  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen  Along the anterior surface is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan white skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm flattened and slightly indurated nipple  Located 2 5cm superior to the nipple is a well healed linear scar measuring 6 5cm in length  The remaining skin surface is pink white and unremarkable  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm attached axillary tail  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black  the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm previous biopsy cavity within the mid portion of the specimen coming to 2 9cm from the overlying unremarkable free moving posterior aspect  4 5cm from the blue inked anterior soft tissue margin and 4 2cm from the scar bearing overlying skin  The cavity is empty and has a dark red to pink  smooth glistening cavity lining  The cavity borders are rubbery with focal areas of fat necrosis  No masses are grossly appreciated  Surrounding the cavity is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm area of dense lobulated pink white fibrous tissue  The remaining parenchyma is tan yellow to pink lobulated and unremarkable with no additional masses or lesions identified  Adjacent to the nipple is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm smooth walled unilocular cystic structure surrounded by slightly indurated fibrous tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm    Within the attached axillary tail  multiple lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in maximum dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of posterior margin closest to cavity taken en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavity wall   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved surrounding dense fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of nipple with cyst   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Four whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One whole lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional axillary fat  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of nipple and surrounding fibrous tissue  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of gray to tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a short black stitch designating the anterior  a long black stitch the lateral  and a bow tie stitch the cephalad margins  The posterior aspect is inked black  the anterior is blue  the superior is green and the inferior is yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm gray pink fibrous  hemorrhagic cavity which communicates with the posterior margin  The cavity is surrounded by abundant chalky tan yellow areas consistent with fat necrosis  Within the cavity wall along the medial half of the specimen is a silver metal clip  A second staple is noted along the mid to lateral portion of the specimen  The remaining cut surface shows dense  rubbery  gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with the cavity as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the tissue bearing the silver metal clips as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Jennifer Nash  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Jennifer Nash  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , Unchecked.
