ARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Not indicated  see prior report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS   2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  1 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  12 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   0 Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x 11 x 2 5cm oriented mastectomy specimen  The anterior surface contains a 3 x 2 5cm skin ellipse and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm nipple  The specimen is oriented with a stitch indicating the 6 o clock position  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial to lateral axis to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm area of soft yellow material located in the central quadrant that is 1 5cm to the closest posterior margin  which is suggestive of caseous necrosis  The remaining breast parenchyma contains abundant amount of tan white rubbery fibrous tissue  No additional discrete mass or lesion is noted  No lymph nodes are present  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative radial section of closest posterior margin to central quadrant lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire central quadrant lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative section from the central quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cross section of nipple  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast   is a 17 x 13 x 2 5cm oriented right mastectomy specimen  The anterior surface contains a REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm unremarkable nipple  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial to lateral axis to reveal a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm firm white mass located in the central to upper outer quadrant  The mass has a white to yellow cut surface and is 4 5cm to the closest posterior margin and 1 0cm to the closest anterior margin  The remaining breast parenchyma contains abundant amount of tan white rubbery fibrous tissue with soft yellow material present in the ducts suggestive of caseous necrosis  No additional discrete mass or lesion is noted  No lymph nodes are present  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of mass to closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of mass to closest anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of mass to surrounding parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cross section of nipple  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right axillary contents   is an 11 x 3 x 1 2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  Twelve candidate lymph nodes are identified ranging in greatest dimension from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 candidate lymph n