rone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 20     FLOW CYTOMETRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm lobular piece of yellow tissue with a needle localization wire  The external surface is inked  Sectioning reveals an ill defined  stellate  white to tan lesion measuring 0 3cm in greatest dimension  The lesion is within 0 1cm of the margin  The portions of the specimen including the nodule are submitted in cassettes A through C  the remainder of the specimen is submitted in cassettes D through G  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS GROSS  LEFT BREAST BX   NO LESION LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS FOR DIAGNOSIS  O R  Resident  Jay Austen  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BX   report_end  , Unchecked.
