 this appearance  The epithelial clusters of concern in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  are no longer present on deeper sections stained for calponin and p63  Dr  Frederick Koerner has reviewed the case and concurs with the interpretation  Multiple levels examined  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  2 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU TUMOR SIZE  Scattered small foci in 3 of 10 blocks  GRADE  1  CALCIFICATIONS  Associated with the carcinoma in situ  atypical changes  and benign changes  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Present at the anterior margin and  0 1cm from the inferior margin  The mucocele like lesion is also present at the posterior margin and  0 1cm from the anterior and superior margins  and re excision of these margins is suggested as well  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on the  lower upper outer quadrant  specimen  the carcinoma has a similar morphology in both specimens   By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  lower upper outer quadrant area of clip   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm piece of yellow fibrofatty tissue  with stitches designating the anterior  lateral  and cephalad  superior  aspects of the specimen per the surgeon  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  superior   green and inferior   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal multiple cysts ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm  and surrounding firm parenchyma  A surgical clip is not grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of remainder of specimen  submitted sequentially