Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 49 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA  THREE MICROSCOPIC FOCI  0 1  REMOVED_DATE  AND REMOVED_DATE CM   PRESENT IN THE WALL OF THE BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE   RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FOCALLY INVOLVING SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  AND FOCALLY PRESENT AT THE ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   Note  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The area of ductal carcinoma in situ that is present at the anterior margin is less than 0 1cm in total size  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 23 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 35                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Lymph Node  Left Axilla   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are two specimens  Labeled  left breast  short superior  long lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm skin ellipse excised a depth of 0 3cm and containing a 2 5cm well healed linear scar  There is a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  a short stitch designating the superior aspect and a double stitch designating the inferior   deep   margin  The anterior aspect is inked in blue while the posterior is inked in black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity with a hemorrhagic  fibrous tract extending to the skin ellipse  There is a firm  tan white  hemorrhagic nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm present in the posterior wall of the biopsy cavity  The cavity is 0 6cm from the posterior inferior margin and 0 6cm from the anterior margin  The rim of stellate fibrosis extends to the posterosuperior and posteroinferior margins  Apparently contiguous with the nodule in the biopsy cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm well circumscribed soft tissue mass with a tan yellow  hemorrhagic rim and brown  variegated center  This nodule is present at the anterior margin and 0 5cm from the posterior margin  Representative sections are taken lateral to medial as follows  SECTION CODE A  Biopsy cavity  nearest  posterior  margin  B  Inferior biopsy cavity  C D  Superior aspect biopsy cavity  E  Fibrous tract to skin from biopsy cavity  F  Inferior aspect biopsy cavity  G  Superior aspect biopsy cavity  H  Hemorrhagic nodule  closest margin anterior  I J  Fibrous areas  Labeled as  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of adipose tissue from which multiple lymph nodes are extracted ranging in size from 0 2cm to 1 2cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes have been submitted in cassettes K through R  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
